ads-cft-link-5cfb4fcf.symmetry_origin:
The AdS/CFT correspondence arises from the study of string theory in specific types of curved spacetimes, namely anti-de Sitter spaces, and their relation to strongly coupled quantum field theories, particularly those with large numbers of colors (N) and large 't Hooft coupling (
  λ
 ). The conformal symmetry of the CFT on the boundary is a key feature, and the duality suggests that this symmetry is intricately linked to the symmetries of the AdS spacetime and the gravitational sector. It is a non-perturbative definition of quantum gravity in AdS space, stemming from the symmetries and dynamics of the dual CFT.

ads-cft-link-5cfb4fcf.limits_and_boundary:
In the limit of a large number of degrees of freedom in the CFT (large 
  N
 ) and strong coupling (
  λ
 ), the gravitational description in AdS becomes classical and reliable. Conversely, in the limit of weak coupling in the CFT, the gravitational description becomes strongly coupled and difficult to analyze. The boundary of the AdS spacetime, where the CFT resides, is crucial; it is a lower-dimensional manifold from which the higher-dimensional bulk geometry can be reconstructed.

